{"id":"word:hebrew:H3707","type":"word","title":"כַּעַס","subtitle":"H3707 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"to trouble ; by implication, to grieve , rage , be indignant","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to כַּעַס (H3707) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: v.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 55 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"כַּעַס (kaʻaç) means to trouble ; by implication, to grieve , rage , be indignant First listed occurrence: 1Kgs 14 9."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"כַּעַס","transliteration":"kaʻaç","pronunciation":"kaw-as'","strong":"H3707","lemmaId":"hebrew:H3707","partOfSpeech":"v","forms":["לְ/הַכְעִיסֽ/וֹ","לְ/הַכְעִיסֵ֔/נִי","לְ/הַכְעִ֗יס","הַכְעִיסֵ֔/נִי","מַכְעִסִ֖ים"],"morphs":[["HR/Vhc/Sp1cs",8],["HR/Vhc/Sp3ms",6],["HR/Vhc",6],["HVhc/Sp1cs",5],["HVhrmpa",4],["HVhp3ms",2],["HC/Vhw3ms",2],["HC/Vqw3ms",2],["HC/Vqq3ms",2],["HVhp3cp/Sp1cs",2]]},"definitions":{"short":"to trouble ; by implication, to grieve , rage , be indignant","usage":"be angry, be grieved, take indignation, provoke (to anger, unto wrath), have sorrow, vex, be wroth.","full":"H3707. kaas כָּעַס verb be vexed, angry (Late Hebrew כָּעַס , Aramaic כְּעַם (not Syriac)); — Qal Perfect ׳כ Psa 112:10 ; Eccl 5:16 ; Imperfect וַיִּכְעַס Nehemiah 3:33; 2Chr 16:10 ; 1 singular אֶכְעַס Ezek 16:42 ; Infinitive לִכְעוֺם Eccl 7:9 . &#8212; 1 be vexed, indignant Psa 112:10 ; Nehemiah 3:33; Eccl 5:16 . 2 be angry Ezek 16:42 ; Eccl 7:9 , with אֶל person 2Chr 16:10 . Piel. Perfect 3feminine singular suffix כִּעֲסַתָּה 1Sam 1:6 ; 3 masculine plural suffix כִּעֲסוּנִי Deut 32:21 provoke to anger. Hiph`il Perfect הִכְעִיס Hosea 12:15; 1Kin 15:30 ; suffix הִכְעִיסוֺ 2Kin 23:26 4 t. Perfect; הַכְעִסֵו֯נִי Jer 25:7 ; (scribal error for תַּכְעִיסוּני according to SS); Imperfect וַיַּכְעֵס 1 Kings 22:54; 2Chr 28:25 ; 3 feminine singular suffix תַּכְעִיסֶנָּה 1Sam 1:7 6 t. Imperfect; Infinitive construct הַכְעִיס 1Kin 16:13 5 t.; suffix הַכְעִ(י)סֵנִי Jer 7:18 11 t., + 6 t. suffixes; Participle plural מַכְעִיסִים 7:19 4 t. — 1 vex , with accusative pers 1Sam 1:7 ; Ezek 32:9 . 2 vex, provoke to anger , especially of provoking Yahweh by workship of other gods Judg 2:12 ; 1Kin 14:9 ; 14:15 ; 16:33 ; 1 Kings 22:54; 2Kin 17:11 ; 23:19 ; 2Chr 28:25 ; Nehemiah 3:37; Jer 7:18-19 , 11:17 ; 32:29 , 32 ; 44:3 ; Ezek 8:17 ; 16:26 ; Isa 65:3 ; Hosea 12:15; with בּ instrumental בְּתוֺעֵבֹת Deut 32:16 ; בְּהַבְלֵיהֶם 32:21 ; 1Kin 16:13 , 26 ; בחטאתם 16:2 ; יד(יוׅ במעשׂ(י) Deut 31:29 ; 1Kin 16:7 ; Jer 25:6-7 , 32:30 ; 44:8 ; ידיהם מעשׂ(ה) בכל 2Kin 22:17 2Chr 34:25 ; בבמות Psa 78:58 ; בפסיליהם Jer 8:19 ; במעלליהם Psa 106:29 ; compare the phrases י בעיני הרע(ה) ׳עשׂה להכעיס(וׅ do the evil in the eyes of Yahweh to provoke (him) to anger Deut 4:25 ; 9:18 ; 31:29 ; 1Kin 16:7 ; 2Kin 17:17 ; 21:6 2Chr 33:6 ; so מכעסים 2Kin 21:15 ; Jer 32:30 ; (יםׅ כעס הכעיס אשׁר 1Kin 15:30 ; 21:22 ; 2Kin 23:26 . &#8212; The phrase is characteristic of D Jeremiah and the compiler of Kings; see Dr Intr 191 ; Deut 4:25 Holz eini. Hexateuch 287 .","rootNote":"a primitive root;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Kgs 14 9","keyReferences":["1Kgs 14 9","1Kgs 14 15","1Kgs 15 30","1Kgs 16 2","1Kgs 16 7","1Kgs 16 13","1Kgs 16 26","1Kgs 16 33"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":55,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Kgs 14 9","book":"1Kgs","chapter":14,"verse":9,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"לְ/הַכְעִיסֵ֔/נִי","source":"hebrew","morph":"HR/Vhc/Sp1cs"},{"reference":"1Kgs 14 15","book":"1Kgs","chapter":14,"verse":15,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"מַכְעִיסִ֖ים","source":"hebrew","morph":"HVhrmpa"},{"reference":"1Kgs 15 30","book":"1Kgs","chapter":15,"verse":30,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"הִכְעִ֔יס","source":"hebrew","morph":"HVhp3ms"},{"reference":"1Kgs 16 2","book":"1Kgs","chapter":16,"verse":2,"e